WEBVTT

NOTE The Line on the Wall. The on-screen words, as captions. Riverton is a fictional city.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Every decision rests on something believed to be true.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:18.200
Four teams. Four decisions. One shared assumption:
the 100-year flood on the east bank stays below 2.4 m.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.000
People move on. Agents keep following the decisions.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.200
Years later, a national flood study: 3.1 m.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.600
The reason stopped being true.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.000
The decisions kept running.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Read: the new study becomes one fact.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.300
Find: nobody said which decisions this touches.
It finds every one that relied on 2.4 m.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.300
Compare: 3.1 m is above 2.4 m. Checked by arithmetic. No model, no guessing.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:59.300
Weigh: a rumour can only raise a question. A strong source can overturn.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.300
Flag: each one is marked at risk, for a person to decide.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.700
One fact changed. It found every decision that depended on it.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:11.100
Before it acts, the agent asks.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:19.200
The answer: stop. This needs a person.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.100
A person sees the evidence, and where it came from.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.800
They decide: accept the evidence, or dismiss it.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.700
And it is on record: what each agent was told, and when.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:37.600
The same line runs under every kind of decision: software, supply, space.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:43.200
DecisionLoop. Decisions, with their reasons, checked against reality.
